@meta
id: 07-15
title: Put the work where your eyes are
chapter: 07
type: lesson
skills: zz-center, goto-line
par: 108
minutes: 8
vscode: scroll a little after every jump so you can see what you are doing
open: refund.provider.ts

@brief
Three review fixes in a 131 line provider. Each one is at a line number you
have been given, and each one needs you to be able to see something other
than the line itself.

  1. Line 48, in `withinWindow`. A negative number of days means the clock
     went backwards and must not count as inside the window. The return
     becomes `return days >= 0 && days <= REFUND_WINDOW_DAYS;`. You want the
     whole three line method visible.

  2. Line 97, in the middle of `settle`. The update needs to record the
     attempt: `values: { status: 'SETTLED', settledAt: new Date(), attempts: 1 },`.
     You want to see what is above and below it.

  3. Line 120, in `reconcile`. Only pending refunds count as missing:
     `const missing = local.filter((refund) => !remote.includes(refund.id) && refund.status === 'PENDING');`
     You want to see the query above it, not the loop below it.

A jump lands you wherever the file happens to leave you — the top of the
screen, the bottom, half a line from the edge. There are three keys that fix
that, and choosing between them is the lesson.

@keys
| `zt` | scroll so the cursor line is at the top of the screen |
| `zz` | scroll so the cursor line is in the middle |
| `zb` | scroll so the cursor line is at the bottom |
| `45G` | line 45 |
| `^` | first non-blank |
| `F)` | back to the previous closing paren |
| `a` `i` | append after, insert before |

@hints
All three are `z` followed by one letter, and the letter says where on the
screen the line you are on should end up. Top, middle, bottom.
--
`zz` centres. It is the one you want by default, and it is worth pressing
after every long jump without even thinking about it. `zt` puts the line at
the top, which is what you want when you have just landed on a function
signature and care about the body underneath. `zb` puts it at the bottom,
which is what you want when the context you need is above.
--
For the first fix, `45G` lands on the method, `zt` pulls the body into view,
and `3j` `^` `w` puts you on `days`. For the other two, jump, set the view,
then `$` `F)` finds the paren you need to write next to.

@solution
    45G zt 3j ^ w i days >= 0 &&  <Esc>
    97G zz $ F ) a , attempts: 1 <Esc>
    120G zb $ F ) i  && refund.status === 'PENDING' <Esc>
    :wq<Enter>

Around ninety-five keystrokes, sixty of them the three fixes.

The grader cannot see the scrolling, and that is worth saying out loud: you
could pass this lesson without pressing `z` once, and you would have learned
nothing. The two keystrokes are for you, not for the file.

Here is why they matter. A jump puts the line you asked for somewhere
arbitrary on the screen. If it lands on the last row, everything you are
about to edit is off-screen and you will scroll by hand, lose your place,
and start clicking. `zz` after a jump costs two keystrokes and means the
line you care about is always in the same place on the screen, with context
on both sides. Fluent vim users press `zz` so often it stops being a
decision — `nGzz` is effectively one motion.

`zt` and `zb` are the same idea sharpened. `zt` is "this is the start of
something, show me the rest of it", which is the right key on a function
signature, a heading, the top of a stanza. `zb` is "this is the end of
something, show me what led to it", which is the right key on a failure, a
closing brace, the last line of a block.

One more, for free: `zz` has a relative you will meet in chapter 17. After
a long jump, `` `` `` takes you back where you came from. Landing, looking
and returning is most of what navigating a codebase actually is.

@start refund.provider.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { RefundRepository } from './refund.repository';
import { OrderRepository } from '../order/order.repository';
import { PaymentService } from '../../infrastructure/services/payment.service';
import { EmailService } from '../../infrastructure/services/email.service';
import { RefundProducer } from './refund.producer';
import {
  CreateRefundArgs,
  FindRefundsArgs,
  ReconcileRefundsArgs,
} from './refund.types';

const REFUND_WINDOW_DAYS = 30;
const MAX_ATTEMPTS = 3;
const MINOR_UNITS = 100;

@injectable()
export class RefundProvider {
  constructor(
    @inject(RefundRepository) protected refundRepository: RefundRepository,
    @inject(OrderRepository) protected orderRepository: OrderRepository,
    @inject(PaymentService) protected paymentService: PaymentService,
    @inject(EmailService) protected emailService: EmailService,
    @inject(RefundProducer) protected refundProducer: RefundProducer,
  ) {}

  public async findOne(args: FindRefundsArgs) {
    const refund = await this.refundRepository.findOne({ where: args.where });

    if (!refund) {
      throw exception('REFUND_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    return refund;
  }

  public async findMany(args: FindRefundsArgs) {
    return this.refundRepository.findMany({
      where: args.where,
      take: args.take ?? 50,
    });
  }

  public withinWindow(placedAt: Date) {
    const days = (Date.now() - placedAt.getTime()) / 86_400_000;

    return days <= REFUND_WINDOW_DAYS;
  }

  public toMinorUnits(amount: number) {
    return Math.round(amount * MINOR_UNITS);
  }

  public async create(args: CreateRefundArgs) {
    const order = await this.orderRepository.findOne({
      where: { id: args.orderId },
    });

    if (!order) {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    if (!this.withinWindow(order.placedAt)) {
      throw exception('REFUND_WINDOW_EXPIRED');
    }

    if (args.amount > order.amount) {
      throw exception('REFUND_AMOUNT_EXCEEDS_ORDER');
    }

    const refund = await this.refundRepository.create({
      orderId: order.id,
      customerId: order.customerId,
      amount: args.amount,
      reason: args.reason,
      status: 'PENDING',
    });

    return refund;
  }

  public async settle(refundId: string) {
    const refund = await this.findOne({ where: { id: refundId } });
    const response = await this.paymentService.refund(
      refund.orderId,
      refund.amount,
      refund.id,
    );

    if (response.status !== 'ok') {
      throw exception('REFUND_FAILED');
    }

    await this.refundRepository.update({
      where: { id: refund.id },
      values: { status: 'SETTLED', settledAt: new Date() },
    });

    await this.refundProducer.settled({ refundId: refund.id });

    return this.emailService.sendReceipt(refund.customerId, refund.id);
  }

  public async retry(refundId: string, attempt: number) {
    if (attempt >= MAX_ATTEMPTS) {
      throw exception('REFUND_FAILED');
    }

    return this.settle(refundId);
  }

  public async reconcile(args: ReconcileRefundsArgs) {
    const local = await this.refundRepository.findMany({
      where: { created: { gte: args.from } },
      take: 1000,
    });

    const remote = await this.paymentService.listRefunds(args.from);
    const missing = local.filter((refund) => !remote.includes(refund.id));

    for (const refund of missing) {
      await this.refundRepository.update({
        where: { id: refund.id },
        values: { status: 'UNRECONCILED' },
      });
    }

    return missing.length;
  }
}

@expected refund.provider.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { RefundRepository } from './refund.repository';
import { OrderRepository } from '../order/order.repository';
import { PaymentService } from '../../infrastructure/services/payment.service';
import { EmailService } from '../../infrastructure/services/email.service';
import { RefundProducer } from './refund.producer';
import {
  CreateRefundArgs,
  FindRefundsArgs,
  ReconcileRefundsArgs,
} from './refund.types';

const REFUND_WINDOW_DAYS = 30;
const MAX_ATTEMPTS = 3;
const MINOR_UNITS = 100;

@injectable()
export class RefundProvider {
  constructor(
    @inject(RefundRepository) protected refundRepository: RefundRepository,
    @inject(OrderRepository) protected orderRepository: OrderRepository,
    @inject(PaymentService) protected paymentService: PaymentService,
    @inject(EmailService) protected emailService: EmailService,
    @inject(RefundProducer) protected refundProducer: RefundProducer,
  ) {}

  public async findOne(args: FindRefundsArgs) {
    const refund = await this.refundRepository.findOne({ where: args.where });

    if (!refund) {
      throw exception('REFUND_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    return refund;
  }

  public async findMany(args: FindRefundsArgs) {
    return this.refundRepository.findMany({
      where: args.where,
      take: args.take ?? 50,
    });
  }

  public withinWindow(placedAt: Date) {
    const days = (Date.now() - placedAt.getTime()) / 86_400_000;

    return days >= 0 && days <= REFUND_WINDOW_DAYS;
  }

  public toMinorUnits(amount: number) {
    return Math.round(amount * MINOR_UNITS);
  }

  public async create(args: CreateRefundArgs) {
    const order = await this.orderRepository.findOne({
      where: { id: args.orderId },
    });

    if (!order) {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    if (!this.withinWindow(order.placedAt)) {
      throw exception('REFUND_WINDOW_EXPIRED');
    }

    if (args.amount > order.amount) {
      throw exception('REFUND_AMOUNT_EXCEEDS_ORDER');
    }

    const refund = await this.refundRepository.create({
      orderId: order.id,
      customerId: order.customerId,
      amount: args.amount,
      reason: args.reason,
      status: 'PENDING',
    });

    return refund;
  }

  public async settle(refundId: string) {
    const refund = await this.findOne({ where: { id: refundId } });
    const response = await this.paymentService.refund(
      refund.orderId,
      refund.amount,
      refund.id,
    );

    if (response.status !== 'ok') {
      throw exception('REFUND_FAILED');
    }

    await this.refundRepository.update({
      where: { id: refund.id },
      values: { status: 'SETTLED', settledAt: new Date(), attempts: 1 },
    });

    await this.refundProducer.settled({ refundId: refund.id });

    return this.emailService.sendReceipt(refund.customerId, refund.id);
  }

  public async retry(refundId: string, attempt: number) {
    if (attempt >= MAX_ATTEMPTS) {
      throw exception('REFUND_FAILED');
    }

    return this.settle(refundId);
  }

  public async reconcile(args: ReconcileRefundsArgs) {
    const local = await this.refundRepository.findMany({
      where: { created: { gte: args.from } },
      take: 1000,
    });

    const remote = await this.paymentService.listRefunds(args.from);
    const missing = local.filter((refund) => !remote.includes(refund.id) && refund.status === 'PENDING');

    for (const refund of missing) {
      await this.refundRepository.update({
        where: { id: refund.id },
        values: { status: 'UNRECONCILED' },
      });
    }

    return missing.length;
  }
}
